From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:08:53 +0200
Subject: Keep Boolean results of nullary case-class unapplies under capture
 checking
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The capture-checking synthetics augmentation ("Two different versions of
unapply types depending on consume", upstream e954236aaf) rewrites a
non-consume case-class unapply's result type to the scrutinee's singleton
x.type. A nullary case class's synthesized unapply returns Boolean, so the
rewrite retypes every `case C() =>` pattern to the scrutinee singleton where
Boolean is required — surfacing, under macro re-splicing or plain rechecking,
as "Found: C^{x} Required: Boolean" (Soundness's mandible Opcode patterns,
anthology's CompilerError). Boolean results are now left unchanged.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude).

Proscala-Patch: boolunapply
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Synthetics.scala | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Synthetics.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Synthetics.scala
index 123abd39d88d614455a9fb72cc72f90844fffdf3..b3f82f574e6cfd6802d24dd67a414c3e0c68397b 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Synthetics.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Synthetics.scala
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ object Synthetics:
           case _ =>
             if paramInfo.hasAnnotation(defn.ConsumeAnnot)
             then CapturingType(tp, CaptureSet.universal)
+            // A nullary case class's synthesized unapply returns Boolean, not the
+            // scrutinee; substituting `x.type` retypes `case C() =>` patterns to the
+            // scrutinee singleton where Boolean is required.
+            else if tp.widenDealias.isRef(defn.BooleanClass) then tp
             else trackedParam
         info.derivedLambdaType(paramInfos = newParamInfo :: Nil, resType = newResult(info.resType))
           .showing(i"augment unapply type $info to $result", capt)
